dwm-reborn
==========

A fork of dwm 6.8 with the sources split into separate translation units and a
horizontal scrolling ribbon instead of the usual master/stack layout. Layout
code lives outside the window manager core, while the user configuration is
still in `include/config.h`.

Highlights:

* one `.c`/`.h` pair per layout in `src/layouts/` and `include/layouts/`;
* `scrolltile` as the default layout: windows are placed sequentially and
  `cyclefocus` pans the visible area;
* `cyclefocus`, `movestack`, `scrollmax`, scratchpad and modal resize;
* `XF86XK_*` media/brightness keys and bindings for the local setup;
* `showbar = 0` by default, so the layout symbol is not drawn.

Requirements
------------

To build you need:

* a C99 compiler (`cc`);
* Xlib, Xinerama, Xft and fontconfig;
* XKB (used by `keypress()`).

Some keybindings expect external programs: `kitty`, `rofi`, `nautilus`,
`maim`, `flameshot`, `magick`, `xclip`, `pactl`, `playerctl`, `brightnessctl`
and `$HOME/.local/bin/xclip-history-menu`. They are not needed for building.

Installation
------------

Paths and flags are defined in `config.mk`. By default:

```text
PREFIX    = /usr/local
MANPREFIX = /usr/local/share/man
```

Build:

```sh
make
```

Install:

```sh
sudo make install
```

This installs:

```text
/usr/local/bin/dwm
/usr/local/share/man/man1/dwm.1
```

Other targets:

```sh
make clean              # remove build/ and the tarball
make dist               # create dwm-6.8.tar.gz
make BUILDDIR=tmp/build # build into another directory
```

Running
-------

A restart-safe `.xinitrc` can be:

```sh
#!/bin/sh
while true; do
    /usr/local/bin/dwm
    [ -f "$HOME/.dwm-exit" ] && { rm -f "$HOME/.dwm-exit"; break; }
    sleep 1
done
```

Restart dwm or the X session after `make install`. To see which binary is
actually running:

```sh
pgrep -a dwm
md5sum /usr/local/bin/dwm build/dwm
```

Configuration
-------------

All user configuration is in `include/config.h`. Rebuild and reinstall after
editing it.

### Layouts

The `layouts[]` array stays in `config.h`. It is wrapped in a guard so that
only one copy exists in the final binary:

```c
#ifdef DWM_CONFIG_LAYOUTS
const Layout layouts[] = { ... };
#else
extern const Layout layouts[];
#endif
```

`DWM_CONFIG_LAYOUTS` is defined only in `src/dwm.c`, before `config.h` is
included. Do not make `layouts[]` static and do not define it in another file:
each copy would have different addresses, and `cyclelayout()` would always
select the first layout.

To add a layout:

1. create `include/layouts/foo.h` with `void foo(Monitor *m);`
2. implement it in `src/layouts/foo.c`
3. include the header from `include/api/layout.h`
4. add an entry to `layouts[]` in `include/config.h`

Currently active layouts:

| Symbol | Layout | Implementation |
| ------ | ------ | -------------- |
| `>>>` | `scrolltile` | `src/layouts/scrolltile.c` |
| `[]=` | `tile` | `src/layouts/tile.c` |
| `[\]` | `dwindle` | `src/layouts/dwindle.c` |

`monocle` and `spiral` are implemented in `src/layouts/monocle.c` and
`src/layouts/spiral.c`, both using `fibonacci.c`. They are commented out in
`layouts[]`.

`cyclelayout(const Arg *arg)` is implemented in `src/api/layoutctl.c`. Bind it
if you want cyclic layout switching:

```c
{ MODKEY, XK_comma,  cyclelayout, {.i = -1 } },
{ MODKEY, XK_period, cyclelayout, {.i = +1 } },
```

`+1` selects the next layout, `-1` the previous one. Entries with
`arrange == NULL` are skipped.

Keybindings
-----------

`MODKEY` is `Mod4Mask` (Super/Win).

### Applications

| Key | Action |
| --- | ------ |
| `Mod+Return` | terminal (`kitty`) |
| `Mod+D` | `rofi -show drun` |
| `Mod+E` | `nautilus` |
| `Mod+V` | clipboard menu |

### Screenshots

| Key | Action |
| --- | ------ |
| `Print` | full screen to clipboard |
| `Ctrl+Print` | selection to clipboard |
| `Mod+Print` | `flameshot gui` |

### Session

| Key | Action |
| --- | ------ |
| `Alt+F4` | close window |
| `Mod+Shift+C` | restart dwm |
| `Mod+Shift+E` | exit session |

### Tags

| Key | Action |
| --- | ------ |
| `Mod+1` … `Mod+0` | view tag |
| `Mod+Ctrl+1` … `Mod+0` | toggle tag in view |
| `Mod+Shift+1` … `Mod+0` | move focused window to tag |
| `Mod+Ctrl+Shift+1` … `Mod+0` | toggle tag on focused window |
| `Mod+Up` / `Mod+Down` | previous/next tag via `shiftview` |

The last tag, `"S"`, is a hidden scratchpad. `shiftview` cycles through all
eleven tags, including `S`.

### Focus and layout

| Key | Action |
| --- | ------ |
| `Mod+Left` / `Mod+Right` | `cyclefocus` |
| `Mod+Shift+Left` / `Mod+Shift+Right` | `movestack` |
| `Mod+Mouse4` / `Mod+Mouse5` | `cyclefocus` |
| `Mod+1` | `scrollmax` |
| `Mod+S` | select `layouts[0]` |
| `Mod+T` | select `layouts[1]` |
| `Mod+F` | toggle floating |
| `Mod+Space` | toggle focus mode |
| `Mod+F11` | toggle fullscreen |
| `Mod+R` | modal resize: `h/j/k/l`, arrows, `Return`/`Escape` |

### Scratchpad

| Key | Action |
| --- | ------ |
| `Mod+Shift+Minus` | `scratchpush` |
| `Mod+Minus` | `scratchshow` |

### Media

`XF86XK_AudioMute`, `AudioLowerVolume`, `AudioRaiseVolume`, `MicMute`,
`Play`, `Pause`, `Prev`, `Next`, `Stop`, `MonBrightnessDown` and
`MonBrightnessUp` are bound to `pactl`, `playerctl` and `brightnessctl`.

Source layout
-------------

```text
include/config.h        tags, keys, layouts, rules
include/api/            public APIs
include/layouts/        layout headers
include/local/          internal headers
include/types/          Monitor, Client, Layout, Drw, ...

src/dwm.c               main; only unit defining DWM_CONFIG_LAYOUTS
src/api/                commands, lifecycle, scrollcompat, movestack, ...
src/layouts/            tile, monocle, fibonacci, dwindle, spiral, scrolltile
src/local/              client, monitor, handlers, geometry, bar, ...
src/renderer/           drw.c
```
